78, 1587, 1633, 1780, 1888, 1999) to a new, different set (e.g. 66, 232, 245, 422, 526, 702, 848, 850, 986, 990, 1317, 1566, 1681). Global summaries for the two half-windows (steps_02 and _03) show comparable overall activity and edge counts, arguing the effect is not an artifact of a big activity collapse or surge. Together this supports an abrupt regime switch centered at \u224823370 rather than gradual turnover across the period."}, "raw_final_response": "{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_798d04c6\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [25, 396, 489, 638, 1036, 1163, 1244, 1366, 1417, 1489, 1729, 1763],\n  \"window\": [18370, 28370],\n  \"confidence\": 0.85,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"The neighborhood-evolution probe (step_01) finds a clear peak change of 1.0 at time 23370, with largely disjoint 'contacts_before_peak' and 'contacts_after_peak' sets. Per-node neighbor lists in the half-windows before (18370\u201323370) and after (23370\u201328370) show that most group members switch from a shared set of old partners (e.g. 65, 74, 163, 292, 442, 880, 978, 1587, 1633, 1780, 1888, 1999) to a new, different set (e.g. 66, 232, 245, 422, 526, 702, 848, 850, 986, 990, 1317, 1566, 1681). Global summaries for the two half-windows (steps_02 and _03) show comparable overall activity and edge counts, arguing the effect is not an artifact of a big activity collapse or surge. Together this supports an abrupt regime switch centered at \u224823370 rather than gradual turnover across the period.\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 62024, "total_output_tokens": 4560, "total_tokens": 66584, "total_latency_ms": 70134, "llm_calls": 18, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}